---
// Lazy: this sits in the sidebar, which phones hide (display:none). An eager
// image downloads anyway, and on the homepage this one was the largest thing
// competing with the phone LCP, the news lead image.
//
// The sidebar is at most ~387px wide (the 4fr of the 1200px grid), so it gets
// 400px and 800px (2x) renditions of the 1080px original (subscribe.webp,
// ~340 KB, kept for anything linking to it directly). width/height are the 1x
// file's, so the slot is reserved before the image arrives.
---
<div class="mb-[8px] overflow-hidden pt-[5px]">
    <a href="/subscribe">
        <img
            class="w-full h-auto"
            src="/images/subscribe-400.webp"
            srcset="/images/subscribe-400.webp 400w, /images/subscribe-800.webp 800w"
            sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 387px, (min-width: 1024px) 300px, (min-width: 640px) 30vw, 100vw"
            width="400"
            height="451"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            alt="Subscribe to The Triangle newsletter: get Drexel news straight to your inbox"
        />
    </a>
</div>
